  "prompt": "Find the common rule that maps an input grid to an output grid, given the examples below. Generate a python script that takes a grid as input and transforms it according to the this rule. Anticipate that this program will be applied to several grids, not only the shown test grid.\n\nYour script must define exactly one callable entrypoint:\ndef solve(grid):\nwhere `grid` is passed as a list of lists of integers (list[list[int]]) and the function returns the transformed grid in the same format.\n\nExample 1:\n\nInput:\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\nOutput:\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 8 6 8 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n6 6 6 1 6 6 6 1 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n8 8 8 1 8 6 8 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput:\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 1 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 1 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 1 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\nOutput:\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8 6 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 8 6 8 1 8 8 6 8 8 8 8\n6 6 6 1 6 6 6 1 6 6 6 6 6 6 6\n8 8 8 1 8 6 8 1 8 8 6 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8 6 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 1 8 6 8 1 8 8\n6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 1 6 6 6 1 6 6\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 1 8 6 8 1 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8 6 8 8 8 8\n\nBelow is a test input grid.\n\nInput:\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 8 8 8 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 1 1 1 1 1 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n\nYour final answer should just be the python script itself, no other text or markdown.",
  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    rects = []\n\n    # Find all hollow rectangles made of 1s\n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            if grid[i][j] == 1:\n                # Check if this is the top-left corner of a rectangle\n                if (i == 0 or grid[i-1][j] != 1) and (j == 0 or grid[i][j-1] != 1):\n                    # Find right edge\n                    r = j\n                    while r + 1 < cols and grid[i][r+1] == 1:\n                        r += 1\n                    # Find bottom edge\n                    b = i\n                    while b + 1 < rows and grid[b+1][j] == 1:\n                        b += 1\n                    # Must be at least 2x2\n                    if b <= i or r <= j:\n                        continue\n                    # Verify bottom edge is all 1s\n                    valid = True\n                    for c in range(j, r+1):\n                        if grid[b][c] != 1:\n                            valid = False\n                            break\n                    if not valid:\n                        continue\n                    # Verify right edge is all 1s\n                    for rr in range(i, b+1):\n                        if grid[rr][r] != 1:\n                            valid = False\n                            break\n                    if not valid:\n                        continue\n                    # Verify interior contains no 1s\n                    for rr in range(i+1, b):\n                        for cc in range(j+1, r):\n                            if grid[rr][cc] == 1:\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                        if not valid:\n                            break\n                    if valid:\n                        rects.append((i, b, j, r))\n\n    # Prepare output grid\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    # Draw the cross for each rectangle\n    for t, b, l, r in rects:\n        cr = (t + b) // 2\n        cc = (l + r) // 2\n        # Horizontal line through center row\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[cr][c] != 1:\n                out[cr][c] = 6\n        # Vertical line through center column\n        for rr in range(rows):\n            if grid[rr][cc] != 1:\n                out[rr][cc] = 6\n\n    return out",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    rects = []\n\n    # Find all hollow rectangles made of 1s\n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            if grid[i][j] == 1:\n                # Check if this is the top-left corner of a rectangle\n                if (i == 0 or grid[i-1][j] != 1) and (j == 0 or grid[i][j-1] != 1):\n                    # Find right edge\n                    r = j\n                    while r + 1 < cols and grid[i][r+1] == 1:\n                        r += 1\n                    # Find bottom edge\n                    b = i\n                    while b + 1 < rows and grid[b+1][j] == 1:\n                        b += 1\n                    # Must be at least 2x2\n                    if b <= i or r <= j:\n                        continue\n                    # Verify bottom edge is all 1s\n                    valid = True\n                    for c in range(j, r+1):\n                        if grid[b][c] != 1:\n                            valid = False\n                            break\n                    if not valid:\n                        continue\n                    # Verify right edge is all 1s\n                    for rr in range(i, b+1):\n                        if grid[rr][r] != 1:\n                            valid = False\n                            break\n                    if not valid:\n                        continue\n                    # Verify interior contains no 1s\n                    for rr in range(i+1, b):\n                        for cc in range(j+1, r):\n                            if grid[rr][cc] == 1:\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                        if not valid:\n                            break\n                    if valid:\n                        rects.append((i, b, j, r))\n\n    # Prepare output grid\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    # Draw the cross for each rectangle\n    for t, b, l, r in rects:\n        cr = (t + b) // 2\n        cc = (l + r) // 2\n        # Horizontal line through center row\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[cr][c] != 1:\n                out[cr][c] = 6\n        # Vertical line through center column\n        for rr in range(rows):\n            if grid[rr][cc] != 1:\n                out[rr][cc] = 6\n\n    return out",
